{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first largest clique: of all the largest cliques, the least by vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ignored. Of two cliques of one size, the lesser is the one holding the least vertex of their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"symmetric difference. After "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cliqueNumber()"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s search, each largest clique is searched for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from its first vertex v in degeneracy order, among v’s later neighbors, so memory stays O(n +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"m + degeneracy²) however large a hub’s degree. For each v, a witness clique W (any one of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the right size) guides a pass over the candidates in ascending number: a candidate in W is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"taken, any other is taken exactly when a search finds the rest of a clique among the common"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neighbors left (which then becomes W). A v whose candidates all exceed the least vertex of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the best clique so far is skipped. Up to one search per vertex and candidate, each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exponential in the worst case, so it can be far slower than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumClique()"},{"type":"text","text":"; the search"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"does not check for task cance